  <completion-notes date="2026-07-22">
    DELIVERED (additive-only — legacy writers/contracts untouched, retired in later tasks 023/032):
    - SERVER: src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/Operations/ComposeOperation.cs — the closed
      set of ten op records (insertText/deleteRange/replaceRange/setMark/clearMark/splitParagraph/
      mergeParagraph/insertParagraph/deleteParagraph/setBlockAttr) as a System.Text.Json polymorphic
      union (`[JsonPolymorphic type]` + `[JsonDerivedType(…, "insertText")]`), anchored by
      ComposeRunPoint{runIndex,offset} / ComposeRunRange{start,end}; envelope ComposeOperationLog
      {schemaVersion, operations}; ComposeOperationSchema.Version = "compose-ops-v1". Pure records; no
      AI internals, no Graph types.
    - CLIENT: src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-operations.ts — the mirror
      discriminated union + COMPOSE_OPERATION_TYPES + isComposeOperation/isComposeOperationLog guards.
      EXTENDS (re-exported from) src/types/compose-contracts.ts + the package barrel src/index.ts — no fork.
    - TESTS: tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/ComposeOperationSchemaTests.cs (4 pass) +
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/types/compose-operations.test.ts (9 pass) —
      round-trip client→server→client byte-stable + wire-discriminator + validation coverage.

    KEY OP-SHAPE DECISION (escalation NOT fired): structural ops (split/merge/insert) reference a second
    paragraph via newParaId/targetParaId carried in the Slate `properties` slot — these are durable
    w14:paraIds (NOT run-ids, NOT absolute positions), so the {paraId,runIndex,offset|range} anchor
    remains sufficient and D2/I-3-compliant. Full rationale + the anchor↔op table:
    projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/task-003-operation-schema-decisions.md.

    VERIFICATION: BFF build green (0 err); server 4/4 + client 9/9 tests pass; Tier-1 NetArchTest
    ADR013_ComposeFacadeTests green; publish 46.11 MB compressed incl PDBs (≤60 ceiling; ~neutral vs
    ~49.63 baseline; zero new runtime package); no NEW HIGH CVE (no .csproj change — pre-existing
