  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-11">The op-type set is a CLOSED union of exactly: insertText, deleteRange, replaceRange, setMark, clearMark, splitParagraph, mergeParagraph, insertParagraph, deleteParagraph, setBlockAttr. Every op is anchored `{paraId, runIndex, offset|range}` and the envelope carries a schema-version field. Scope: identical shape on client and server.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / D2">The durable anchor is `(paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset)`; the schema MUST NOT use run-*ids* or absolute editor positions as the durable anchor. Scope: offsets are run-local; run boundaries are resolved at patch time (not encoded as durable ids).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">The server contract in `Services/Compose/Operations/` MUST inject/reference NO AI-internal type (`IOpenAiClient`/executor/routing) — Tier-1 NetArchTest stays green. Scope: pure records; the AI redline path produces ops via the facade, not here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">No `Microsoft.Graph` type in the operation contract. Scope: the schema is transport-agnostic bytes-and-anchors, not a Graph type.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The schema is the SINGLE source both ends validate against; a serialized op log MUST round-trip client→server→client without loss. Scope: add round-trip validation tests (server unit + client Vitest).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §11">EXTEND the existing `src/types/compose-contracts.ts`; do NOT create a parallel/duplicate contracts module on the client. Scope: `compose-operations.ts` augments, it does not fork.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Shared client/server operation contract; Slate discriminated-union op shape; paraId+runIndex+offset anchor; facade discipline (no AI internals)</topic>
